Add /dev/mgbe_zc 4x25GbE zero-copy TP=2 backend behind dsv41/rdma.Ring for Jetson AGX Thor.

Plugs /dev/mgbe_zc (CUDA VMM CU_MEM_LOCATION_TYPE_HOST_NUMA single-region staging + 4-rail
VDMA 2 eager / VDMA 3 SPH=1 hardware DDP) behind dsv41/rdma.Ring so dsv41_rdma.cu and
dsv41_shard.cu (sendRows/recvRows) run unchanged with full CUDA-Graph and PDL support.
Also routes prefill/Engram/head gathers through Ring.gatherChunked when mgbe_zc is active
(leaving DGX Spark RoCE + NCCL behavior unchanged) and adds mgbe_zc mode to tf-dsv41-rdma-bench.

Switches (both ranks):
  TF_MGBE_ZC=1|0 (default: auto when TP=2 on Linux and no RDMA devices)
  TF_MGBE_ZC_MAX_KB (default: 20480, 20 MiB per rank)
  TF_MGBE_ZC_EAGER_KB (default: 32, per-rail eager vs DDP threshold)
  TF_MGBE_ZC_PORTS, TF_MGBE_ZC_CPUS, TF_MGBE_ZC_TIMEOUT_S, TF_MGBE_ZC_ARRIVAL_TIMEOUT_S, TF_MGBE_ZC_DEBUG

